.TH OBCR 6 "November 2026" "OBCR 1.0.0-beta.2" "Games"
.SH NAME
obcr \- Operation Body Count source port
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B obcr
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B obcr \-\-check\-data
\fIdir\fR|\fIimage\fR
.br
.B obcr \-\-extract\-data
\fIsource\fR \fIdir\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B obcr
is a native source port of Operation Body Count (Capstone Software, 1994),
written in Rust on SDL 3 and rebuilt from the original executable. It plays
the original game tic for tic from the user's own copy of the game files,
in the original 320\(mu200 picture (Classic) or at high resolution and in
widescreen with smooth motion, xBRZ textures, modern controls, gamepads and
UDP network play (Enhanced).
.PP
The game data is not included. Both the floppy release (\fBCOUNT.EXE\fR) and
the CD release that Steam and GOG sell as a BIN/CUE image (\fBBCCD.EXE\fR)
are recognized by the SHA\-256 of their files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-data " dir"
The folder with the game files.
.TP
.BI \-\-check\-data " dir" | image
Identify a copy of the game (a folder, or a \fI.cue\fR, \fI.bin\fR or
\fI.iso\fR image), print one tab\-separated line per file, and exit with 0 if
every required file matches a known release, 2 if not.
.TP
.BI \-\-extract\-data " source dir"
Copy the files the game uses from a folder or CD image into \fIdir\fR,
ripping the CD music (\fBTRACK02.QOA\fR to \fBTRACK05.QOA\fR) from an image.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Use \fIfile\fR as the settings file; saved games go to \fIsaves\fR beside it.
.TP
.B \-\-classic
The original 320\(mu200 picture.
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " n"
Enhanced resolution multiple, 2 to 8.
.TP
.BI \-\-aspect " ratio"
Enhanced aspect: \fB4:3\fR, \fB16:10\fR, \fB16:9\fR or \fB21:9\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-xbrz " n"
xBRZ factor for textures, 2 to 6, or 0 for the original texels.
.TP
.BR \-\-xbrz\-menus " on|off, " \-\-xbrz\-hud " on|off"
xBRZ for menus, pictures and movies; for the status bar.
.TP
.BR \-\-floors " smooth|original"
Floors and ceilings in true perspective, or as the original drew them.
.TP
.BR \-\-fullscreen ", " \-\-windowed
Start fullscreen or in a window.
.TP
.B \-\-nsr250
The original's cheat parameter: Alt+Left Shift+B in game turns on bogus mode.
.TP
.BR \-\-net " N|T|M"
Start a network game: deathmatch, teams, or two players.
.BR \-\-net\-join " host[:port]"
calls a player (repeatable),
.BI \-\-net\-port " port"
sets the UDP port (default 16387),
.BR \-\-net\-choice " 0|1|2"
picks the character or team, and
.B \-\-net\-setup
opens the setup screen instead of starting at once.
.TP
.BI \-\-play " n"
Start directly on map slot \fIn\fR (0\-based), with
.BI \-\-difficulty " n"
(0\(en2 difficulty 1\(en3, 3 Random).
.TP
.BI \-\-sequence " name"
Play one animated sequence (\fBF1\fR to \fBF7\fR) and quit.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-\-version
The full list of options, and the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OBC_DATA_DIR
The game data folder, used when \fB\-\-data\fR is not given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/obcr/obcr.toml
Settings, written on exit. See \fIdocs/options.md\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/obcr/saves/
Saved games.
.TP
.I ~/.local/opt/OBCR/
Where OBCR Setup installs the game, with the game files in \fIdata/\fR.
